      "final_text": "Done \u2014 `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` on all 8 requirements, and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n**The bug:** `OzSqrt.sqrt` in [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) ran only 6 Newton steps instead of the deployed 7, so large inputs (e.g. `2^256 - 1`, `2^204 - 1`) converged short of the floor root. Fix: added the seventh `(result + a / result) >>> 1` line, matching `newtonSqrt 7`.\n\n**The proof** (same file, `namespace OzSqrt`):\n- `sqrt_toNat`: `(sqrt a).toNat = Nat.sqrt a.toNat`. Lifts each word step to `ProofForgeFin.Sqrt.newton` on values (initial estimate via `toNat_log2` + `toNat_one_shiftLeft_bv`; step 0 by direct non-overflow, steps 1\u20137 via `toNat_newton_word_of_sqrt_le` with all iterates under `2^130`), then applies `newtonIter_eq_or_succ_of_lt_two_mul` (b=128, k=5, i.e. 5+2=7 steps) plus `min_div_eq_sqrt`.\n- `sqrtUp_toNat`: the rounded-up root on values, with exactness of the squaring and the `+1`.\n- The 8 required theorems follow: `req_sqrt_not_above`/`req_sqrt_not_below` from `Nat.sqrt_le`/`Nat.lt_succ_sqrt`; `req_sqrt_up_covers`/`req_sqrt_up_tight` from the library's rounded-up-root lemmas; `req_mint_backed`/`req_mint_full`/`req_mint_live` via `firstMint_eq_some`/`firstMint_isSome`; `req_newton_budget` with `k = 7` by unfolding.\n\nPassport: `.proofforge/passport-001.json` (`727e4813\u2026aba06`); executable property tests pass (2001 cases, 0 violations); only permitted axioms (`propext`, `Quot.sound`, `Classical.choice`).",
